  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules set a 24-hour serious-incident reporting duty and a 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger that applies to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), but the 5% test failure rate only triggers a corrective-action plan, so no model is ever required to stop sales. Per-model numerical failure rates go to regulators and to purchasers before purchase, but not to the general public, and the six-year retrofit window protects Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. The 36-month lead time on new-unit shut-off falls outside the 12-month acceptable range in the code's rules, which is why S3 is rated weakened."
 },
